  "result": "I looked through the app first. Right now the site reads `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night, and shows it as the timetable. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no way to show a warning. So the warning itself is easy to add. The harder part is how the site finds out about a cancellation in the first place.\n\n**When a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that decision get made, and who finds out first?**\n\nI'm asking because the answer decides most of what gets built. If cancellations are usually known the day before, they could come in through the nightly export. If they happen on the day, because of weather or a breakdown, a file that updates overnight would be too late. Then someone at the office would need a quick way to flag the sailing directly.\n\nOr if you'd rather I just dive in, say so.",
